  "description": "ONATII crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C73 H82 N4 O19 Tm4,C6 H16 N1 1+,2(C4 H10 O1),N1 O3 1-. From the CIF bond table, Tm1 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm2 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm3 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm4 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.446-3.797 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.76-110.12°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C73H82N4O19Tm4·C6H16N·NO3·2(C4H10O) (table C87H118N6O24Tm4). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
